<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105147" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπλ-όος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπλ-πλοῦς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆ</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>triple, threefold,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλλίνικος ὁ τ.,</span> because this hymn
			of victory was <i>thrice repeated,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				9.2
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τ. ἁμαξιτοῖς,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τριόδῳ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				716
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. ζεῦγος,</span> of persons,
				<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				773.61
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄνομα τ.</span>”
				<i>compounded of three,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1457a34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπλοῦν ἀποτινέτω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PRev.Laws</u>
					19.14
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰσπράξαντα τριπλῆν τὴν πρᾶξιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMich.Zen.</u>
					71.7
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόριον τ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.58
				</span></i>
			; 
				Att.
			 neut. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπλᾶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					1033
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				792
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πλῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Procl.
					<u>in Prm.</u>
					p.656S.
				</span></i>
			; 
				gloss on 
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριχθά</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				<u>Epim.</u>
				134
			</span></i>: but dat. fem. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριπλῇ</span> is
			used as Adv. in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.128
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Pseudol.</u>
				32
			</span></i>.</div>
